# Read by GitHub ("Cite this repository") and by Zenodo when a release is
# archived. Before the release: add each author's ORCID as
#   orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
# (Zenodo rejects the file if an ORCID is malformed, so leave the line out
# rather than use a placeholder), and set version and date-released to match
# the release tag. After the DOI is minted, add it as `doi:`.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or these methods, please cite them as below."
type: software
title: "CCR_ROV_survey_methods: ROV survey methods, field operations and imagery software"
abstract: >-
  Hardware configuration, field workflow and open-source software used by the
  Seattle Aquarium's Coastal Climate Resilience (CCR) team for standardized
  benthic imaging surveys with a small, modular remotely operated vehicle
  (BlueROV2) in temperate kelp forests. Includes two Windows desktop
  applications, ROV Flight Operations (field operations, navigation,
  telemetry health and transect extraction) and ROV Imagery Processing
  (photo import, RAW development and telemetry-annotated video), the
  mcap_to_csv transect extractor, ArduSub Lua scripts, a lighting-control
  subsystem, a printable field log, and the code and data behind the
  associated survey-methods manuscript.
